# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: aldo-companion-quit-leaks-a-host-backtrace — (quit) at a debugger prompt killed the process with a host backtrace
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-sedit-path-and-alfe-list-hosts
#+DATE: 2026-09-26

* Observed

Found 2026-09-26 while MEASURING =navi-double-quit= on the built binary (a
separate ticket; that one does not reproduce, see its note). Typing =(quit)= at
the debugger prompt:

#+begin_example
$ printf '(defun foo (x) (/ x 0))\n(foo 1)\n(quit)\n' \
  | clautolisp -norc -q --on-error debug
...
NAV>
Unhandled CLAUTOLISP.AUTOLISP-RUNTIME:AUTOLISP-TERMINATION in thread
  #<SB-THREAD:THREAD tid=3381742 "aldo-companion" RUNNING>:
  AutoLISP termination requested: QUIT
 5: ((LAMBDA (&REST ARGUMENTS) :IN WRAP-BUILTIN-FUNCTION))
14: ((LAMBDA NIL :IN CLAUTOLISP.TOOLS.CLAUTOLISP::START-ALDO-COMPANION))
15: ((LABELS BORDEAUX-THREADS::%BINDING-DEFAULT-SPECIALS-WRAPPER ...))
...
22: ("foreign function: funcall1")
unhandled condition in --disable-debugger mode, quitting
$ echo $?
1
#+end_example

Twenty-two frames of host Lisp, and exit 1, for a user asking the program to
end. At the =_$= prompt the same form prints =clautolisp: terminated by QUIT=
and exits 0.

* Cause

The debugger UI runs on the *aldo companion thread* (=start-aldo-companion=,
tools/clautolisp/source/main.lisp). Its handler-case round =session-stop=
caught =error= only -- and =AUTOLISP-TERMINATION= is defined as a
=SERIOUS-CONDITION=, not an =ERROR= (autolisp-runtime/source/api.lisp:172),
deliberately, so that a quit is not mistaken for a failure. So the condition
left the companion thread unhandled, and the host Lisp killed the process.

This is the class AGENTS.md § /Architecture/ forbids: "Common Lisp conditions
and errors must not leak directly into the AutoLISP environment."

The companion cannot simply return from the handler: the application thread is
parked at the stop waiting for a resume directive, so there is nobody to hand
the termination to -- and the user asked for the program to END, not for the
stop to resume.

* Fixed — clautolisp 2.2.116

=COMPANION-TERMINATE= reports the termination with the toplevel's own
=report-termination= (so a quit from the debugger and a quit from =_$= do not
look like two different events), flushes the streams, and ends the process with
the status the form carried. The exit function is injectable, which is what
makes it testable without exiting the test run. The companion's handler-case
gained a clause for =autolisp-termination= ahead of the =error= one.

Measured after the fix, on the BUILT binary:

#+begin_example
(quit)   at the NAV> prompt -> "clautolisp: terminated by QUIT", exit 0
(exit 3) at the NAV> prompt -> "clautolisp: terminated by EXIT", exit 3
                               (with its [exit-status-extension] dialect warning)
zero host-backtrace lines in either
#+end_example

Tests (tools/clautolisp/tests/debugger-options-tests.lisp):
=companion-terminate-reports-and-exits-with-the-forms-status= checks the wording
and that the injected exit is called with the form's status;
=companion-terminate-is-reached-for-a-termination-not-an-error= pins the reason a
separate clause is needed -- if =autolisp-termination= ever became an =ERROR=
subtype, the companion's error clause would swallow a quit and answer
=:continue=, and that test fails instead of the user's session.

Documented in the user manual (the aldo section: quitting from a stop) and
RELEASE_NOTES.org.

* Note

Filed and fixed in the same change, per AGENTS.md: a bug found while doing
something else gets its own ticket, and an implemented-and-tested issue is
closed with the code.
